&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;12+ years of enterprise partnerships, alliances, or business development experience, with meaningful time spent on partner ecosystems&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven track record of building and scaling partnerships with systems integrators, consultancies, or channel partners&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience building a co-sell or channel motion from the ground up, including the commercial mechanics behind it&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deep understanding of how cloud and partner field organizations operate, and the incentives that drive seller and partner behavior&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Track record of carrying and hitting a partner-sourced or partner-influenced revenue number, with credible forecasting behind it&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong executive presence and demonstrated ability to influence senior stakeholders where you have no formal authority&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellence in strategic planning, business operations, and program management&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to balance strategic thinking with tactical execution, and a willingness to concentrate effort rather than spread thin&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working with technical products and translating complex capabilities into business value&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to travel up to 25% of the time&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Previous experience working with AWS or another hyperscaler partner organization&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Working knowledge of systems integrator operating models, including practice structures, delivery economics, and how services revenue drives partner decisions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Background in AI/ML technologies or with developer-focused platforms and their partner ecosystems&lt;/li&gt;
