&lt;p&gt;Anthropic’s mission is to create reliable, interpretable, and steerable AI systems. We want AI to be safe and beneficial for our users and for society as a whole. Our team is a quickly growing group of committed researchers, engineers, policy experts, and business leaders working together to build beneficial AI systems.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h2 class=&quot;heading&quot;&gt;About the role&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Anthropic&#39;s Beneficial Deployments team exists to ensure AI&#39;s benefits reach the people and communities that markets typically leave behind. As our work in Economic Mobility builds momentum, we&#39;re hiring a partnerships manager dedicated to career pathways in the AI age.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You&#39;ll lead Claude Corps, our $150M flagship early career program — a national fellowship placing 1,000 early-career fellows, paid full-time for a year, with nonprofits serving communities across the U.S. Designed and run with CodePath, you&#39;ll own the program&#39;s success through its first cohorts and its evolution into replicable workforce infrastructure for the field if the program is impactful for both fellows and nonprofit host organizations.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Beyond Claude Corps, you&#39;ll grow our talent developer partnerships — building on momentum like our CodePath partnership that infuses Claude and Claude Code in courses that reach 20,000+ students at community colleges, universities and workforce programs across the country. You will also lead workforce-related deployments on AI Fluency and Claude fluency with national and regional partners, helping workers build the skills to shape their own pathways in the AI transition.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is program and partnership leadership with real stakes on a global scale. The economic mobility field is early in its AI journey, and the organizations we work with choose Anthropic because of values alignment. You&#39;ll earn and keep that trust by delivering measurable results by supporting millions of people and their pathways through our partners by 2027. The role rewards entrepreneurial orchestration: building new programs amid ambiguity, scaling what works, and enabling partners to manage mature programs so you can build what&#39;s next.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2 class=&quot;heading&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Key responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Lead Claude Corps end-to-end&lt;/strong&gt; — cohort launches, host organization pipeline, coordination with CodePath, program measurement, and the open-source playbook&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Develop and close tier-1 partnerships&lt;/strong&gt; with talent developers, workforce organizations, and philanthropic and public sector partners — from scoping and structuring through deployment, measurement, and scale&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Deploy AI Fluency workforce development offerings&lt;/strong&gt; for states and cities, and drive adoption of AI Fluency and Claude fluency training with national and regional partners&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Orchestrate across functions&lt;/strong&gt; — working with Anthropic Academy, Economic Research, Applied AI, Policy, Communications, and GTM teams inside Anthropic, and with funders and agencies outside it&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Understand what works through research and share through open, replicable models&lt;/strong&gt; the broader workforce field can use&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;You may be a good fit if you:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Have personally structured and led large, multi-year, multi-stakeholder partnerships&lt;/strong&gt; — corporate, nonprofit, or public sector — and can speak to outcomes you advanced, not just agreements you signed&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Have operated inside a large or fast-growing company&lt;/strong&gt; — on a people, talent, or HR team, or as a sponsor of talent and early career programs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Have real substance in AI fluency, technical training, or learning programs&lt;/strong&gt; — you have built, deployed, or led training and talent development work, not just advised on it&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Build well amid ambiguity&lt;/strong&gt; — you create structure where none exists, adapt quickly when programs shift, and prioritize execution for impact over process&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Communicate at an executive level&lt;/strong&gt; — your writing is exec-ready, you are a confident public speaker, and you move fluidly between corporate, nonprofit, and government audiences&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Strong candidates may also have:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience designing learning programs end-to-end&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;An existing network across workforce development, philanthropy, or the public sector&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hands-on fluency with Claude — workflows, tools, or assets you have personally built&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
