&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Anthropic&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Anthropic’s mission is to create reliable, interpretable, and steerable AI systems. We want AI to be safe and beneficial for our users and for society as a whole. Our team is a quickly growing group of committed researchers, engineers, policy experts, and business leaders working together to build beneficial AI systems.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h2&gt;About the role&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Anthropic&#39;s mission depends on our people being able to do their work wherever that work needs to happen. Global Mobility is what makes that possible.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This role is the operational heart of that work. You will be responsible for business travel compliance at Anthropic — business visas, posted worker and social security obligations, and documentation that get our people across borders — together with the entity transfers that move employees between our legal entities as the company grows. You will also support the rest of our mobility programs: relocations, international assignments, and short-term placements, along with the project work that comes with them as they grow.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Key responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Own business travel compliance cases end to end.&lt;/strong&gt; Business visas, PWD, Social Security registration. You decide what a case needs, work the documentation to ground, and get people where they are going. Novel fact patterns will land on your desk without precedent. You research it, form a view, and check it with your manager before we commit.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Support employees through relocations and assignments.&lt;/strong&gt; You are the person they come to from the day they accept to the day they arrive. You initiate cases with our providers, keep the move on track, and answer the questions people have when they are moving their life to another country.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Own the experience of every entity transfer.&lt;/strong&gt; You execute the process end to end, and you hold the experience: the employee always knows where things stand, stakeholders such as Payroll, People Services, and Legal have what they need before they ask, and nothing falls between systems. A transfer can be a big moment in someone&#39;s working life. Your work is what makes it feel seamless.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Be the first line for global mobility questions.&lt;/strong&gt; Employees, hiring managers, and recruiters come to you first. You answer most of it yourself, escalate the genuinely novel, and turn the questions you keep getting into documentation so you stop getting them.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Hold our providers to their commitments.&lt;/strong&gt; You will know their process well enough to tell what they cannot do from what they simply have not done yet — and you will say so, in a relationship forward manner.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Pick up the project work as our programs grow.&lt;/strong&gt; You handle the exceptions, so you see the patterns before anyone else: a policy that needs rewriting because the same case keeps coming up, a new provider to implement, a country we have not sent anyone to before. Scoped with your manager, run by you.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong data-pm-slice=&quot;3 3 [&amp;quot;paragraph&amp;quot;,{}]&quot;&gt;Minimum qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Have worked in global mobility.&lt;/strong&gt; We do not expect expertise across business visas, relocation, &lt;em&gt;and&lt;/em&gt; mobility tax. We do expect that you have personally owned cases and can walk us through one.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Are relentlessly responsive.&lt;/strong&gt; You treat employees and colleagues as people navigating a stressful moment, not as tickets. You close loops before anyone has to chase you.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Explain complicated things simply.&lt;/strong&gt; You can make a visa process legible in writing, quickly, and without jargon.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Look for the repeatable thing inside the manual thing.&lt;/strong&gt; You have made your own work faster before, and you would rather build the fix than absorb the pain.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong data-pm-slice=&quot;3 3 [&amp;quot;paragraph&amp;quot;,{}]&quot;&gt;Preferred qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with entity transfers, business travel compliance including PWD filings, or Social Security notifications&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with Workday, Greenhouse, or Jira&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hands-on experience using Claude or other LLM tooling in their daily work&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience at a startup growing quickly, where the process is not always written yet&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-pay-transparency&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-input&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;description&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;The annual compensation range for this role is listed below.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;For sales roles, the range provided is the role’s On Target Earnings (&quot;OTE&quot;) range, meaning that the range includes both the sales commissions/sales bonuses target and annual base salary for the role.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;title&quot;&gt;Annual Salary:&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-range&quot;&gt;&lt;span&gt;$135,000&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;divider&quot;&gt;&amp;mdash;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;$180,000 USD&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Logistics&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Minimum education: &lt;/strong&gt;Bachelor’s degree or an equivalent combination of education, training, and/or experience&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Required field of study:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;A field relevant to the role as demonstrated through coursework, training, or professional experience&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Minimum years of experience: &lt;/strong&gt;Years of experience required will correlate with the internal job level requirements for the position&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Location-based hybrid policy:&lt;/strong&gt; Currently, we expect all staff to be in one of our offices at least 25% of the time. However, some roles may require more time in our offices.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong data-stringify-type=&quot;bold&quot;&gt;Visa sponsorship:&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;We do sponsor visas! However, we aren&#39;t able to successfully sponsor visas for every role and every candidate. But if we make you an offer, we will make every reasonable effort to get you a visa, and we retain an immigration lawyer to help with this.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;We encourage you to apply even if you do not believe you meet every single qualification.&lt;/strong&gt; Not all strong candidates will meet every single qualification as listed.&amp;nbsp; Research shows that people who identify as being from underrepresented groups are more prone to experiencing imposter syndrome and doubting the strength of their candidacy, so we urge you not to exclude yourself prematurely and to submit an application if you&#39;re interested in this work. We think AI systems like the ones we&#39;re building have enormous social and ethical implications. We think this makes representation even more important, and we strive to include a range of diverse perspectives on our team.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong data-stringify-type=&quot;bold&quot;&gt;Your safety matters to us.&lt;/strong&gt; To protect yourself from potential scams, remember that Anthropic recruiters only contact you from&amp;nbsp;@anthropic.com&amp;nbsp;email addresses. In some cases, we may partner with vetted recruiting agencies who will identify themselves as working on behalf of Anthropic. Be cautious of emails from other domains. Legitimate Anthropic recruiters will never ask for money, fees, or banking information before your first day. If you&#39;re ever unsure about a communication, don&#39;t click any links—visit&amp;nbsp;&lt;u data-stringify-type=&quot;underline&quot;&gt;&lt;a class=&quot;c-link c-link--underline&quot; href=&quot;http://anthropic.com/careers&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; data-stringify-link=&quot;http://anthropic.com/careers&quot; data-sk=&quot;tooltip_parent&quot; data-remove-tab-index=&quot;true&quot;&gt;anthropic.com/careers&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/u&gt;&amp;nbsp;directly for confirmed position openings.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;How we&#39;re different&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We believe that the highest-impact AI research will be big science. At Anthropic we work as a single cohesive team on just a few large-scale research efforts. And we value impact — advancing our long-term goals of steerable, trustworthy AI — rather than work on smaller and more specific puzzles. We view AI research as an empirical science, which has as much in common with physics and biology as with traditional efforts in computer science. We&#39;re an extremely collaborative group, and we host frequent research discussions to ensure that we are pursuing the highest-impact work at any given time. As such, we greatly value communication skills.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The easiest way to understand our research directions is to read our recent research. This research continues many of the directions our team worked on prior to Anthropic, including: GPT-3, Circuit-Based Interpretability, Multimodal Neurons, Scaling Laws, AI &amp;amp; Compute, Concrete Problems in AI Safety, and Learning from Human Preferences.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Come work with us!&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Anthropic is a public benefit corporation headquartered in San Francisco. We offer competitive compensation and benefits, optional equity donation matching, generous vacation and parental leave, flexible working hours, and a lovely office space in which to collaborate with colleagues. &lt;strong data-stringify-type=&quot;bold&quot;&gt;Guidance on Candidates&#39; AI Usage:&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;Learn about&amp;nbsp;&lt;a class=&quot;c-link&quot; href=&quot;https://www.anthropic.com/candidate-ai-guidance&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; data-stringify-link=&quot;https://www.anthropic.com/candidate-ai-guidance&quot; data-sk=&quot;tooltip_parent&quot;&gt;our policy&lt;/a&gt; for using AI in our application process.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Anthropic&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Anthropic’s mission is to create reliable, interpretable, and steerable AI systems. We want AI to be safe and beneficial for our users and for society as a whole. Our team is a quickly growing group of committed researchers, engineers, policy experts, and business leaders working together to build beneficial AI systems.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are hiring a Global Power Delivery Equipment Lead to own Anthropic&#39;s global strategy, OEM relationships, and capacity position for long-lead power equipment that sets the pace of Anthropic&#39;s global data center build-out. You will stand up and lead Anthropic&#39;s global equipment strategy function and represent Anthropic with OEM executives, utilities, and development partners. In this role, you will own end-to-end sourcing strategies for critical power generation and grid-integration equipment — gas turbines, reciprocating engines, large power and generator step-up transformers, medium- and high-voltage switchgear, solar and battery energy storage (BESS), and related balance-of-plant electrical — across both off-grid (behind-the-meter, islanded, bridge power) and grid-integrated sites.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The scope is global: you will cover all regions (US, EMEA, APAC) and coordinate with the regional energy leads so that equipment strategy, OEM capacity reservations, and allocation decisions are made once, at portfolio scale, rather than project by project. The sourcing strategy you build should also make innovative power system approaches buildable — off-grid, solar-dominant configurations (solar + BESS with firming generation), not just conventional gas + grid. You will partner closely with energy origination, engineering, demand planning, construction, legal, finance, and third-party development partners to drive equipment availability, establish OEM relationships, and negotiate framework and commercial agreements.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Drive commercial negotiations and framework / Master Purchase Agreements for critical power equipment such as gas turbines (simple and combined cycle), reciprocating engines, fuel cells, large power and generator step-up transformers (HV/EHV), medium- and high-voltage switchgear, substation and protection equipment, solar, and battery energy storage systems.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Secure and manage OEM manufacturing slots and capacity reservations — reservation agreements, deposits, slot allocation, delivery milestones, warranties, liquidated damages, and assignment rights — and run the allocation and reallocation process across sites and regions as deals are signed.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Build and hold relationships with OEM headquarters and regional leadership across North America, Japan and Asia, and Europe, including on capacity-expansion and allocation commitments.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Own the global power equipment strategy: translate the site and energy pipeline into equipment forecasts and procurement pipelines for both off-grid and grid-integrated configurations, and keep the equipment pipeline view (reserved / on order / in fabrication / allocated) current.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Enable innovative power system approaches — off-grid, solar-dominant configurations (solar + BESS with firming) alongside conventional gas + grid — by securing the OEM relationships, reservations, and framework terms that make them buildable at scale and on schedule.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Set the global equipment plan with the regional energy leads in the US, EMEA, and APAC so regional generation strategy, interconnection timelines, and local code and grid requirements are reflected in what is bought, when, and for where.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Decide allocation across sites and partners in constrained markets, hold partners to schedule, and own total cost of supply.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Implement frameworks for ensuring third-party data center partners, EPCs, and general contractors adhere to commercial equipment terms and technical specifications, including owner-furnished equipment (OFE) assignment and reimbursement mechanics.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Work with EPC and power producer / utility counterparties on collaborative sourcing and programmatic equipment approaches — joint or pooled orders, standardized specs, and framework buys that span sites and counterparties — so equipment is bought as a program rather than deal by deal, drawing on utility sourcing practices where they fit.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Own lead-time risk across the portfolio, directing EPCs, development partners, and regional energy leads on lead-time management for long-lead power equipment — tracking OEM lead times and delivery schedules against site and project schedules and deciding order timing and slot allocation and reallocation across sites and counterparties — so equipment lands when each site needs it.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Proactively monitor global supply chain volatility (e.g., lead times and capacity for turbines, transformers, and switchgear; country-of-origin and tariff exposure) and execute contingency plans and alternative-source strategies to avoid critical project delays.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Track the energy-innovation, energy-to-data-center integration, and domestic-manufacturing and global-trade dynamics that move power-equipment availability and cost — new generation and storage technologies, behind-the-meter and grid-integrated delivery models, OEM capacity expansion, tariff and country-of-origin exposure — and turn them into sourcing positions.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Own the commercial structure (deposits, payment schedules, credit support, capital deployment) with Finance and Legal and carry transactions through executive approval.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Partner with power-system design and engineering early — site power architecture, generation mix, interconnection approach — so equipment sourcing strategy and system design inform each other rather than sourcing arriving after the design is fixed; and on specifications and standardization so equipment purchased on-spec can be redeployed across sites, regions, and development partners.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Negotiate warranty, startup/commissioning support, long-term service, and spare parts terms, and track OEM performance.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;You may be a good fit if you:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Have 12+ years in power equipment, grid infrastructure, or energy markets, spanning at least two of: OEM commercial or business development; utility or power-producer sourcing and development; renewables or storage development; procurement or EPC — including having led a function, team, or portfolio-scale program.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Have a track record of developing processes for forecasting, planning, and procuring power generation and grid-integration equipment for data centers, utilities, IPPs, or large industrial loads.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Are familiar with power systems equipment (e.g., gas turbines, reciprocating engines, fuel cells, large power and GSU transformers, MV/HV switchgear, protection and substation equipment, solar, BESS) and the differences between islanded/behind-the-meter and grid-connected configurations.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Have direct experience negotiating framework, master supply, or capacity reservation agreements with major power-equipment OEMs.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Are familiar with utility sourcing practices — framework and alliance agreements, reservation and blanket orders, standard specifications, and OEM qualification programs — and can adapt them to a programmatic equipment approach.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Have negotiated framework or reservation agreements at $100M+ scale with executive-level OEM relationships.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Have worked inside or directly with a major power-equipment OEM (transformers, HV/switchgear, grid automation, turbines) on commercial structures, capacity allocation, and new business models.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Have presented strategy and risk to executive leadership or a board.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Have worked alongside power-system design engineers on site power architecture, generation mix, and interconnection, and can translate between what the system needs and what the OEM market can deliver.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Possess a bachelor&#39;s degree in a relevant domain (e.g., electrical engineering, power systems, construction management, supply chain) or equivalent practical experience.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;It&#39;s a bonus if you have:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;5+ years experience in data center, utility, or critical environment power infrastructure.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Experience sourcing across multiple regions (US, EMEA, APAC) and working with regional OEM sales, EPC, and logistics organizations.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Established relationships with major generation, transformer, and switchgear OEMs and familiarity with their slot-allocation processes.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Experience working with general contractors, EPCs, MEP integrators, OEMs, and equipment distributors on data center construction programs.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Familiarity with interconnection processes and utility/ISO requirements relevant to large loads and on-site generation.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Familiarity with battery energy storage systems and hybrid generation architectures.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Experience with OEM warranty, return, repair, and replacement programs.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-pay-transparency&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-input&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;description&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;The annual compensation range for this role is listed below.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;For sales roles, the range provided is the role’s On Target Earnings (&quot;OTE&quot;) range, meaning that the range includes both the sales commissions/sales bonuses target and annual base salary for the role.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;title&quot;&gt;Annual Salary:&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-range&quot;&gt;&lt;span&gt;$320,000&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;divider&quot;&gt;&amp;mdash;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;$405,000 USD&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Logistics&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
