&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Serve as a key strategic advisor to our life science research teams on complex research, development, and commercial matters globally&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive high deal volume with life science and biopharma counterparties across a range of sophisticated agreement types&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify, analyze, and proactively manage life science regulatory risks in close coordination with the broader Legal department&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design and implement scalable guidance and processes to support our fast-growing life science efforts&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Anticipate emerging legal developments affecting AI technologies in the life science and biopharma space and provide strategic guidance to leadership&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Minimum qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;JD and active membership in at least one U.S. state bar (California or New York preferred)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Real fluency in how the life sciences industry works: how drugs get developed, how research organizations are structured, what pharmaceutical and biotech counterparties care about, and why&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Working knowledge of the regulatory environment life sciences tools may be deployed in — GxP, clinical and health data regulations, human-subjects research, FDA processes&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deep experience with negotiating and drafting complex IP allocation issues in multi-party research arrangements, including ownership of inventions and improvements&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent communication skills, with the ability to translate legal risk into practical guidance for scientists, researchers, and business partners&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience scoping and managing outside counsel across specialties (FDA/regulatory, IP, privacy, export control) for both substantive depth and cost efficiency&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Exceptionally collaborative disposition - with the ability to find creative solutions that account for multiple priorities at once&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A low-ego, high-empathy orientation and a &quot;doer&quot; attitude — willing to roll up your sleeves and pitch in where needed&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Intense curiosity about AI and science, and a commitment to responsible AI development&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;10+ years of relevant legal experience, including substantial experience in life sciences transactional work — contract research, strategic collaborations, and licensing and commercialization deals — with the ability to operate independently and hit the ground running&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with AI/ML companies or products deployed into regulated scientific and clinical settings, particularly for drug discovery&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with biosecurity, dual-use research, or export control considerations in the life sciences&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience leveraging AI to optimize their work, with a desire to work in a fast-paced, innovative environment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Scientific or technical training&lt;/li&gt;
