&lt;p&gt;You will make Claude Tag successful on new surfaces, including working with early adopters, customizing the core interaction paradigm for the surface, designing delightful onboarding, and working with external partners. You should be equally comfortable building relationships with top customers to inform the product evolution, debugging a permissions bug or model behavior with engineers, and presenting product strategy to executives.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Responsibilities:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Define Claude Tag&#39;s core interactions on the surface, tailoring the interaction model to fit the surface.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the strategy and roadmap for bringing Claude Tag to new collaboration surfaces beyond Slack&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the external partnerships that make those surfaces possible, from first conversation through shipped integration&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own adoption from design partners to scaled rollout at the largest companies&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You might be a good fit if you:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Have a combined 8+ years in product management, or equivalent experience driving product direction&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Have shipped platform integrations or ecosystem products, and owned the partner relationship&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Have strong instincts for multiplayer and collaborative product design, where the experience is shared and public rather than private&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Have a strong grasp of model capabilities and work fluently with engineering teams on technical products. An engineering background is not required&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Are energized by ambiguity and bring structure to it rather than waiting for it&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Have a creative, hacker spirit and love solving puzzles&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;San Francisco and Seattle only&lt;/p&gt;
